<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 21-30 June, sterling's average RMG is greater than +5 per cent at 5.240. It will Btherefore enter the first of up to five 10-day confirmation p eriods tomorrow, 1 July, prior to a possible revaluation on 20 August. The next largest RMG is that of the Italian lira at 2.571 per cent. The negative threshold is therefore -2 per cent (the minimum possible). As there are no currencies with average RMGs below this threshold, all green rate changes will remain unchanged tomorrow, the beginning of the first confirmation period running  from 1 - 10 July. With the resumption of the confirmation process, the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is s</p>
